# Responsive Design Rule

- Treat responsiveness as a default requirement for all UI changes.
- Build mobile-first layouts, then enhance with breakpoint utilities.
- Avoid fixed widths/heights unless there is a clear requirement; prefer fluid sizing.
- Use responsive spacing, typography, and layout behavior across common breakpoints.
- Ensure interactive controls remain usable on small screens.
- When adding or updating components, verify behavior in small, medium, and large viewports.
